MAG (Mapping Guideline):
------------------------
Purpose:
Defines how to transform data from a source message (defined by a MIG) to a target message (also defined by a MIG).
Usage:
Used in the mapping step of an integration application to map fields between different message structures.
Example:
Mapping fields from a purchase order IDoc to a corresponding purchase order in a different format.
Key Features:
Specifies the mapping logic between source and target message structures.
Can include XSLT scripts for complex mappings.
Can be based on source and target message implementation guidelines.
Provides guidance for implementing mapping in the integration application.


where can we find MIG/MAG
--------------------------

-> Check your SAP Cloud Integration License:
Ensure you have an enterprise edition license, as Integration Advisor is not available with the standard edition.

-> Access the SAP BTP Cockpit:
Log in to your SAP BTP Cockpit.

-> Find the "Process Integration" Service:
Locate the "Services" section and then choose "Process Integration".

-> Configure Process Integration:
Click on "Configure Process Integration" within the "Take Action" screen area of the Process
Integration service page.

-> Access the Integration Suite:
You'll find the Integration Suite tile and can subscribe to it.

-> Navigate to Subscriptions:
Within the Integration Suite, you'll find the "Subscriptions" section where you can manage your
subscriptions, including Integration Advisor.

-> Access the Integration Advisor Application:
Once subscribed, you'll be able to access the Integration Advisor application, which includes the
Type System library and other features.